  "ethnobotanical_info": "Willows are a significant resource to many Indigenous Tribes of California. They serve as material for weaving baskets and constructing traditional houses, sweat lodges, fences, and arrow shafts. Medicinally, willow bark contains a bitter salicyclic acid used to treat fevers and headaches, reduce inflammation, and relieve pain. Aspirin is a commonly used synthetic derivative of this compound. A remedy of its roots is used to relieve diarrhoea.",
